ls/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/28.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/29.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/3.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/30.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/31.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/32.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/33.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/34.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/35.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/36.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/37.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/38.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/39.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/4.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/5.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/6.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/7.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/8.log", "Blind Trials/22_02_2026/Evening/2026_02_22_16_54_49_0/9.log", "Blind Trials/blind_detection_log.txt", "Blind Trials/blind_detection_results.csv", "Blind Trials/blind_detection_scored_aps.csv", "LICENSE", "README.md", "Scripts/__pycache__/rogue_localizer.cpython-313.pyc", "Scripts/__pycache__/visualize_results.cpython-313.pyc", "Scripts/blind_hotspot_detector.py", "Scripts/parse_logs.py", "Scripts/plot_downsampling_single.py", "Scripts/robustness_studies.py", "Scripts/rogue_localizer.py", "Scripts/visualize_results.py", "Scripts/zone_strip_blind.py", "device_summary.csv", "downsampling_study.csv", "downsampling_summary.csv", "figures/aggregate_results.pdf", "figures/aggregate_results.png", "figures/blind_trials_map.pdf", "figures/blind_trials_map.png", "figures/downsampling_study.png", "figures/downsampling_study_single.pdf", "figures/downsampling_study_single_preview.png", "figures/error_comparison.pdf", "figures/error_comparison.png", "figures/interactive_map.html", "figures/map_overview.pdf", "figures/map_overview.png", "figures/session_error_cdf.pdf", "figures/summary_table.pdf", "figures/summary_table.png", "figures/zone_strip.pdf", "figures/zone_strip.png", "map.pgm", "map.yaml", "parsed_rssi.csv", "results.csv", "results_aggregate.csv", "summary.csv"], "readme": "# RogueRover\n\nAutonomous rogue wireless-device localization for incident response, using a single commodity quadruped robot. The robot autonomously patrols a pre-mapped facility, collects spatially labeled RSSI measurements over a standard 802.11 interface, and estimates device locations offline, without RF fingerprinting, pre-installed sensors, or site calibration.\n\nThis repository releases the measurement data, analysis code, and a demonstration video to support reproducibility of the paper *\"RogueRover: Autonomous Rogue Device Localization for Incident Response.\"*\n\n<!-- After your first Zenodo release, paste the [REDACTED] it gives you here:\n[REDACTED]\n-->\n\n## Artifacts\n\n- **Code and data:** this repository.\n- **Archived release (citable):** `https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20706941`\n- **Demonstration video:** `[10.5281/zenodo.20706771](https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21755919)`\n\n## Summary of the study\n\n- Platform: Unitree Go2 quadruped, ROS 2 Foxy, LiDAR-based autonomous navigation.\n- Sensing: dual 802.11n interfaces; `wlan0` passive 2.4 GHz scanning, `wlan1` robot comms.\n- Protocol: 39-waypoint route (~3.4 m spacing), Stop-and-Scan, 10 s dwell per waypoint.\n- Environment: ~800 m\u00b2 single-floor office; 11 patrols over four days; 6 rogue APs across open, drywall, and glass-partitioned zones.\n- Headline result: 1.62 m median single-patrol localization error without prior RF knowledge; five of six APs within 1 m under multi-patrol aggregation.\n\n## Repository layout\n\n```\ndata/\n  patrols/          # per-patrol RSSI logs (one CSV per run)\n  ground_truth.csv  # measured true AP positions (x, y)\n  whitelist.csv     # authorized-infrastructure BSSIDs/SSIDs\nsrc/\n  detection.py      # heuristic rogue-scoring (LAA bit, SSID patterns, vendor lookup)\n  preprocess.py     # 25 dB session filter; max-RSSI-per-waypoint fusion\n  localization.py   # WCL, ExpWCL, LS+Huber, Ensemble estimators\n  evaluate.py       # reproduces Table 1 and the figures\nfigures/            # generated output\n```\n\n## Measurement schema\n\nEach row in `data/patrols/*.csv`:\n\n| column     | description                                   |\n|------------|-----------------------------------------------|\n| bssid      | observed BSSID                                |\n| rssi       | received signal strength (dBm)                |\n| channel    | 802.11 channel                                |\n| interface  | scanning interface                            |\n| timestamp  | observation time                              |\n| x, y       | robot's localized position at the waypoint (m)|\n\n## Reproducing the results\n\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\npython src/evaluate.py --data data/ --out figures/\n```\n\nThis regenerates the single-patrol error table and the per-AP and downsampling figures.\n\n## Citing\n\nIf you use this dataset or code, please cite the paper. See `CITATION.cff`.\n\n## License\n\nCode is released under the MIT License (see `LICENSE`). Measurement data is released under CC-BY-4.0; please attribute the paper when reusing it.\n", "readme_present": true, "readme_scrub": {"leaked": true, "hits": {"badge_image": 1, "badge_word": 1}}, "signals": {"dependency_manifest": [], "container": [], "build_script": [], "ci_config": [], "licence": ["LICENSE"], "tests": []}, "readme_referenced_paths": ["detection.py", "evaluate.py", "ground_truth.csv", "localization.py", "preprocess.py", "requirements.txt", "src/evaluate.py", "whitelist.csv"], "pushed_at": "2026-08-02T07:18:37Z", "created_at": "2026-06-15T12:45:29Z", "stars": 0, "archived": false}